TESTING:
--------
Tested on macOS 14.5 (Darwin 24.5.0) with:
- Buffers up to 6GB (well beyond old 2GB limit)
- SMB mount I/O (real-world network buffering)
- Rate-limited output to verify buffer fill behavior
- All three binaries compile cleanly

Test commands:
  # Basic functionality
  dd if=/dev/zero bs=1m count=1000 | ./mbuffer -m 3G | dd of=/dev/null
  
  # Verify buffer behavior
  dd if=/dev/zero bs=1m count=10000 | ./mbuffer -m 2G -v 3 -R 100m | dd of=/dev/null
  
  # Real-world SMB usage
  tar cf - /path/to/smb/mount | ./mbuffer -m 5G | tar xf - -C /destination

COMPATIBILITY:
--------------
- Requires C99 for 64-bit long long type
- Uses standard pthread mutexes and condition variables
- macOS-specific code properly conditionally compiled (#ifdef __APPLE__)
- Maintains backward compatibility with existing command-line options
- No changes to public API or command-line interface

