+From 90495240522a71a5ce3be05a5111d82ba5d73ecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: stlalpha <spaceman@themcbros.com>
+Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2025 12:31:11 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] Fix idev.so and tapetest.so compilation on macOS
+
+The configure script's objdump-based symbol detection doesn't work on
+macOS (Mach-O binary format), leaving LIBC_OPEN, LIBC_READ, LIBC_WRITE,
+and LIBC_FSTAT macros empty in config.h.
+
+This causes compilation failures in idev.c and tapetest.c when the
+preprocessor expands function names to nothing.
+
+Solution:
+- Detect when these macros are empty using the existing ISEMPTY() macro
+- On macOS (__APPLE__), define them to the correct symbol names:
+  - _open (not open)
+  - _read (not read)
+  - _write (not write)
+  - _fstat (not fstat)
+- On other platforms, use unprefixed names or error out
+
+Changes:
+- idev.c: Add conditional symbol definitions after macro declarations
+- tapetest.c: Replace #error directives with conditional macOS handling
+- Both: Use TOSTRING() macro for dlsym() calls to get correct symbol names
+
+Result:
+All three components now compile cleanly on macOS:
+- mbuffer (main binary)
+- idev.so (I/O interception library)
+- tapetest.so (tape device emulation library)
+
+Warnings about macro redefinition are expected and harmless - they confirm
+we're overriding the empty config.h definitions with the correct values.
