+Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Add macOS support via condition variables and
+ platform-specific improvements
+
+This commit combines two fixes to enable full macOS compatibility:
+
+## 1. Replace POSIX semaphores with condition variables (from previous merge)
+
+Previous implementation used POSIX semaphores (sem_t, sem_init, sem_post,
+sem_wait, sem_getvalue) for producer-consumer synchronization. This had
+two major limitations:
+
+- macOS does not implement sem_init() for unnamed semaphores (returns ENOSYS)
+- Semaphore counters are 32-bit (INT_MAX), limiting buffer size to
+  sysconf(_SC_SEM_VALUE_MAX) * Blocksize (~2GB typically)
+
+Replaced with pthread condition variables + 64-bit volatile counters:
+- counter_init/wait/post/getvalue functions in common.c
+- FreeBlocks/FullBlocks counters with FreeMut/FullMut mutexes
+- FreeCond/FullCond condition variables for signaling
+- Removes semaphore dependency entirely (macOS compatible)
+- Removes buffer size limitation (64-bit counters)
+
+Modified files: globals.h/c, common.h/c, mbuffer.c, input.c, settings.c
+
+## 2. macOS-specific platform improvements (this commit)
+
+Added macOS-specific code for optimal operation:
+
+- Memory detection using Mach VM APIs (host_statistics64)
+  Calculates available pages from free + inactive + purgeable + speculative
+  Eliminates "unable to determine number of available pages" warning
+
+- fsync error handling for APFS and other macOS filesystems
+  Added EOPNOTSUPP and ENOTSUP as expected errors in terminateSender()
+  and terminateOutputThread() since some macOS filesystems don't support sync
+
+- Updated README to document full macOS support
+  Replaced "does not compile" notice with compatibility documentation
+
+- Bug fix: Removed extraneous strerror(errno) from warningmsg() call
+
+## Result
+
+mbuffer now compiles and runs on macOS with no external dependencies beyond
+POSIX threads. Buffer sizes beyond 2GB are supported. All functionality tested
+on macOS with buffers up to 5GB.
