+Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Fix idev.so and tapetest.so compilation on macOS
+
+The configure script's objdump-based symbol detection doesn't work on
+macOS (Mach-O binary format), leaving LIBC_OPEN, LIBC_READ, LIBC_WRITE,
+and LIBC_FSTAT macros empty in config.h.
+
+This causes compilation failures in idev.c and tapetest.c when the
+preprocessor expands function names to nothing.
+
+Solution:
+- Detect when these macros are empty using the existing ISEMPTY() macro
+- On macOS (__APPLE__), define them to the correct symbol names:
+  - _open (not open)
+  - _read (not read)
+  - _write (not write)
+  - _fstat (not fstat)
+- On other platforms, use unprefixed names or error out
+
+Changes:
+- idev.c: Add conditional symbol definitions after macro declarations
